(function(){var C=window.__CLIPS||(window.__CLIPS={});var d={"Press Begin when you are ready.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Worked example.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Yes.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Not quite yet. Have another look, or use a hint.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Not quite yet. That's fine. You can try again, or move on without an answer.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Choose an answer first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Type your answer first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Put all of them in order first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Sort all of them first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You explored new possibilities.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "New idea explored.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You worked through something difficult.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Challenge explored.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You stayed with the challenge.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Strong persistence.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You tried a different approach when your first idea did not work.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "New strategy discovered.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You kept trying.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Learning continued.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You looked carefully before deciding.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Careful observation.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Solving conflict through mediation.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Today I am practising how a mediator helps people solve a conflict fairly.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What is mediation?.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Mediation is when a calm, fair person helps two people solve their conflict. The mediator does not take sides.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "The steps.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Agree to the rules. Each person tells their side without interrupting. The mediator repeats what they heard. Together they brainstorm solutions and agree on a fair one.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Lerato and Musa both claim the class computer at break. How would a mediator help?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Set the rules, then let Lerato and then Musa explain without interrupting.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Repeat back: \"You both want the computer at break.\"": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Brainstorm: share time, take turns on different days, or work together. They agree on Lerato Monday, Musa Tuesday.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What does a good mediator do?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Listens to both sides without taking sides": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Decides who is right": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Takes their friend's side": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Tells them both to go away": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "A mediator is fair.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "They help people solve it themselves.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "They don't pick a winner.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "A mediator listens to both sides fairly and helps them find their own solution.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Put the mediation steps in order.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Rules come first so everyone feels safe.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Then each person speaks.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Ideas come before the final agreement.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Rules, each side, brainstorm, then agree.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Sort these: peacekeeping skills or not?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Peacekeeping skills help people agree.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Which ones make people feel respected?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Interrupting, blaming and name-calling make conflict worse.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Listening, taking responsibility and co-operating are peacekeeping skills.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Why does the mediator repeat what each person said?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "To check they understood correctly": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "To embarrass them": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "To waste time": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "To take sides": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Misunderstandings cause conflict.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Repeating shows you listened.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "It checks that you got it right.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Repeating back checks understanding and shows each person they were heard.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "During a mediation, one learner threatens to hurt the other. What should the mediator do?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Stop and get an adult straight away": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Carry on as if nothing happened": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Choose a side": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Leave them alone": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Is anyone unsafe?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Some problems need adult help.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Safety comes first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Safety comes first. The mediator should stop and get an adult straight away.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Which peacekeeping skill is your strongest?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Listening": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Staying fair": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Finding solutions": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Not sure": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Fair solutions help everyone feel respected.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Mediator. a fair person who helps others solve a conflict.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Neutral. not taking sides.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Agree. both people say yes to the same solution.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,"};for(var k in d)C[k]=d[k];})();
